.\" cstk.1 - Manual page for CyberSecurityToolKit
.TH CSTK 1 "2026-09-28" "CSTK 3.0.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cstk \- run the CyberSecurityToolKit launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo cstk
.br
.B sudo cstk
.RI [ "global option" ]
.br
.B sudo cstk
.I class-option tool-option
.br
.B sudo cstk
.I combined-short-option
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cstk
is the main launcher for CyberSecurityToolKit (CSTK), a collection of
security assessment, payload-development, post-exploitation, and supporting
utilities.
Running
.B cstk
without arguments opens the interactive menu. Tools can also be selected
directly by combining a class with a tool option.
.PP
CSTK requires root privileges. Use it only on systems, accounts, networks,
and data for which you have explicit authorization. Several payload and
post-exploitation options can alter files, credentials, services, or system
availability.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-H
Display the short help and examples.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display the complete command help generated from the launcher.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-V
Display the short version string.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display the full version string.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-check-updates
Refresh package metadata and report the update status of CSTK-managed system
packages and repositories. Python and Go tools are listed for resolution by
the explicit update command. Nothing is installed.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-update
Check the recorded CSTK-managed system packages, pipx applications, and
GitHub or Go tools, display the scope, and ask for confirmation before
installing updates. System-package updates are limited to packages recorded
by the CSTK installer; this option does not perform a full distribution
upgrade or automatically remove packages.
.IP
After a CSTK self-update, the current trusted launcher requests the private
integrity refresh key and rebuilds and verifies the protected checksum
manifest before executing the updated launcher.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-private-data
Open the interactive private-data manager for the invoking user. It can
reapply private permissions, copy legacy shared Bank files without overwriting
existing private files, create an unencrypted tar archive, or create a
password-protected 7-Zip archive with encrypted filenames.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-tty
Display the guide for upgrading a basic Linux shell to a full TTY.
.TP
.B \-\-control {engagements|inventory|tcp-connect}
Invoke the separately installed loopback-only CSTK Local Control client as the
original invoking user. The client uses that user's private API token and
supports only fixed command contracts; it is not an arbitrary command runner.
.PP
CSTK never contacts update servers during ordinary launcher startup. Updates
must be checked or installed explicitly with the options above or through the
interactive main menu.
.SH COMMAND FORM
Short class and tool options may be combined. For example,
.B \-On
selects the OSINT class and its Nmap helper.
.PP
Long options are supplied separately. The equivalent long command is:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo cstk \-\-osint \-\-nmap
.RE
.PP
Supplying a class without a tool displays the available tools for that class.
