attack tools. The operator selects an OpenAI-compatible endpoint and model;
remote endpoints must use HTTPS, redirects are refused, and API keys are read
from operator-selected environment variables or a hidden session-only dialog
rather than stored. Its safety
display shows provider/model and engagement status. Engagement context is
withheld unless the phase-two record is active, and proposed questionnaire or
scope changes remain review-only.
.SH INTEGRITY MANAGEMENT
The installer creates
.I Other/SecurityChecks/sha256.checksum
after installing CSTK and its wrapper. The manifest covers the launcher,
uninstaller, internal verifier, executable tools, library files, and the
wrapper when it is present.
.PP
The checksum file is installation-specific and is intentionally excluded from
Git. CSTK verifies it before interactive and direct tool execution. If the
manifest is missing or a protected file has changed, CSTK refuses to launch a
tool and offers either a safe exit or permanent removal of the launchers and
core program files. Removal requires a second explicit confirmation and
preserves private user data, legacy Bank files, logs, wordlists, and installed
packages.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B sudo cstk
Open the interactive CSTK menu.
.TP
.B sudo cstk \-On
Run the OSINT Nmap helper using combined short options.
.TP
.B sudo cstk \-\-osint \-\-sweep
Run the fast IP sweeper using long options.
.TP
.B sudo cstk \-Pn
Open the Netcat payload workflow.
.TP
.B sudo cstk \-\-postx \-\-browser
Open the browser-data collection workflow.
.TP
.B sudo cstk \-\-etc \-\-hashid
Open the hash-identification helper.
.TP
.B sudo cstk \-Ei
Open CSTK AI Analyst in interactive configuration mode.
.TP
.B sudo cstk \-\-private-data
Manage private Loot, Malware, and runtime Logs folders, change the runtime
logging preference, or create a backup.
.TP
.B sudo cstk \-\-control engagements
List engagement records through the optional local control API.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/cstk
Global symbolic link to the CSTK launcher.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/cstk_wrapper
Restricted wrapper that supplies the internal tool execution environment.
.TP
.I scripts/lib/cstk_wrapper
Version-controlled wrapper template installed and refreshed by CSTK maintenance commands.
.TP
.I scripts/bin/
Executable CSTK tools and platform-specific helper programs.
.TP
.I scripts/lib/
Documentation, encrypted payload resources, templates, and supporting data.
.TP
.I scripts/lib/cstk.1
Source manual page installed by
.BR install.sh .
.TP
.I Other/SecurityChecks/sha256.checksum
Locally generated integrity manifest. This file is not committed to Git.
.TP
.I /etc/cstk/lib_decryption.key
Root-owned, mode 0600 key used to decrypt protected CSTK library resources.
The key is provisioned by the installer and is never stored in the repository.
.TP
.I Other/Wordlists/
Wordlists supplied with or retained for CSTK.
.TP
.I data/
Locally downloaded breached email and password data. This directory is not
committed to Git.
.TP
.I $HOME/.local/share/cstk/Loot/
Per-user collected assessment results. The directory uses mode 0700.
.TP
.I $HOME/.local/share/cstk/Malware/
Per-user generated payloads and other potentially dangerous output. The
directory uses mode 0700.
.TP
.I $HOME/.local/share/cstk/Logs/
Per-user runtime tool logs. The directory uses mode 0700. Basic logging is the
default. Full logging is opt-in and may include credentials, targets, command
arguments, and complete tool output.
.TP
.I $HOME/.local/share/cstk/Keys/
Per-user generated keys and sensitive cryptographic material. The directory
uses mode 0700 and is included in user-requested private backups.
.TP
.I $HOME/.local/share/cstk/.logging_enabled
Per-user runtime logging preference: off, basic, or full. The file uses mode 0600.
.TP
.I $HOME/CSTK-Exports/
User-requested private backups. Archive files use mode 0600. Unencrypted
.B .tar.gz
and password-protected
.B .7z
formats are available.
.TP
.I Bank/Loot/ and Bank/Malware/
Legacy shared output folders. CSTK no longer writes new output here; the
private-data manager can copy their contents without deleting the originals.
Keep them until migration and backup have been checked.
.TP
.I log/
Installer, updater, and uninstaller maintenance logs. Runtime tool logs are
stored in the invoking user's private Logs directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CSTK_MAIN_RUNNER
Set internally when the main launcher authorizes a wrapped tool.
.TP
.B CSTK_WRAPPER_RUNNER
Set internally by the restricted wrapper before invoking a helper.
.TP
.B CSTK_LIB_KEY_SOURCE
Used only by
.BR install.sh
to provision the library decryption key from a protected regular file without
placing the key on the command line.
.TP
.B CSTK_USER_DATA_DIR
Per-user data root, normally
.IR $HOME/.local/share/cstk .
.TP
.B CSTK_LOOT_DIR
Per-user Loot output directory.
.TP
.B CSTK_MALWARE_DIR
Per-user Malware output directory.
.TP
.B CSTK_LOG_DIR
Per-user runtime tool log directory.
.TP
.B CSTK_KEYS_DIR
Per-user generated-key directory.
.TP
.B CSTK_LOGGING_ENABLED
Compatibility name for the per-user runtime logging level.
.TP
.B CSTK_LOGGING_LEVEL
Per-user runtime logging level: off, basic, or full.
.TP
.B CSTK_USER_HOME
Absolute home directory of the account that invoked CSTK.
.TP
.B home_dir
Exported by the launcher as the absolute CSTK installation directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested action completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
A general, integrity, or tool execution error occurred.
.TP
.B 2
Root privileges are missing or the command-line arguments are invalid.
.PP
Individual tools may return additional nonzero status codes.
.SH INSTALLATION
Run
.B sudo bash install.sh
from the CyberSecurityToolKit directory. The installer places a compressed
copy of this manual under
.I /usr/share/man/man1/
and updates the manual-page index. After installation, display it with
.BR "man cstk" .
