.SH ENGAGEMENTS
Use -G or --engagements to create, select, validate, and manage engagements.
Use --use ID to select an active engagement for this process.
Main menu G provides guarded TCP checks and bounded HTTP(S) requests.
The live status area displays scope, authorization, operational status, and
emergency contact. Unsupported legacy tools are blocked in engagement mode.
Main menu L requires explicit LAB confirmation for unguarded standalone use;
it is unavailable inside a selected engagement session.
Every guarded destination and redirect is authorized before connection.
This is an application-level guard, not a host firewall or network shaper.
